# Python Virtual Environment

Use only `venv/` at the workspace root. Never system `python` / `pip`.

```bash
venv/bin/python <script>
venv/bin/pip install <package>
venv/bin/uvicorn app.api.main:app --reload --port 8001
venv/bin/pytest unit_test/
```

Python 3.10+. Keep `requirements.txt` and `setup.py` pins in sync. Tests live under `unit_test/` (not only `tests/`). Use `GRAPHYN_SKIP_PLUGIN_LOAD=1` for isolated unit tests when plugins are irrelevant.
